[Music]  hi I'm Evan Carmichael welcome to  another edition of ask Evan in today's  episode I'm going to answer a question  from one of my readers John who has  launched a couple books there are  children's books and now he's about to  launch his third and it's had a couple  issues with his publisher where they  haven't been able to sell the first two  books and his warning how can he sell  those two books before launching the  third book so John thanks for the  question I'm researching the process of  creating my own book  so spoiler alert for some of you guys so  it's definitely an interesting process  from the research that I've done I've  seen the publishers typically will give  a lot of support to an author in terms  of helping you edit the book and get it  on a timeline and you can get it into  bookstores but they don't do a lot of  promotion after the fact and a lot of  that relies on the author table to do  that themselves so what a lot of authors  have told me is they'll get you into the  bookstore and maybe do a little launch  party but that's it the rest is on you  dot you go and promote so how you can do  that intelligently the first thing I do  is try to launch a blog tour so find all  the different bloggers who talk about  children's books or children a lot of  the mommy bloggers give them a copy of  the book let them review it and offer to  do an interview or some kind of review  on their blog and trying to line up a  whole series of those you want to try to  get blogs who have a loyal following  people who are active so look for ones  that have a lot of comments on it and  are tightly tied to your community in  this case children and so if you can  line up one of those so try to line up  say one a week for the next year you get  52 bloggers you know talking about uh  promoting your book and maybe doing an  interview it just depends on the style  of the blog that helps get your name out  there a little bit more especially as  they build momentum a lot of people will  read one blog and another blog on  another blog of it spies for similar  interests so if they see you constantly  appearing in all these different blogs  the more they see you the more likely  they're going to you know become  familiar with you and the more like  they're gonna want to buy your book so  if it's a review of your book or if it's  interview with the blogger whatever  format best fits the blogger I try to  get out there and and get seen instead  of this block through yourself the  second thing you do is be a meteor  expert for whatever type  you know message you're sending out  there so it's children's books which is  great  there may be an underlying theme to some  of your books usually in books that  cover you know some kind of theme  whether it's manners or bullying or  whatever it is you know going goodnight  whatever those topics are you could be  seen as almost an expert so when media  are writing about those types of stories  if they need experts to come on  you can go on and talk about it and talk  about your book and why you created this  book and how you hope that it can help  with bullying or you know whatever issue  again you're covering in in your book  itself a great service that I use is  called PR leads and everyday reporters  basically send their list of stories  that they're working on that they're  looking for experts on so every story  people are looking for experts so why  can't you be that expert so anything  related to children if the theme fits  your book you could go on and say you're  the author of this book you have an  interesting story to tell and you know  you might be a potential fit for that  story so something I look at peer leads  isn't free it's $100 a month but I used  to get into New York Times and Forbes  and some pretty big publications and you  know hopefully you'll be able to do it  too for you know anything related to  children and so those are some some  quick tips the last thing I would do is  get a website going I don't know if you  have a website or not you didn't include  it but you know maybe there's a site for  your books I try to get those going  because if people like the book then you  can have a newsletter to then sign  people up so when you have your new book  coming out you know they can hopefully  want to also buy it as well I know there  there are some books that my son likes  to read that we want to have everyone in  the series so whenever the author  publishes a new one and we want to know  what that new book is so we can go out  and get it as well add to the collection  because he loves it so much so if you  had a website where people can sign up  with a newsletter and be notified many  new books coming out that would be  fantastic so you can go on your blog too  or immediate or promoting the first book  and second book and drop hints about the  third book and collect people's email  addresses on your website so then when  you are ready to launch you have a whole  list of people to immediately start  boosting sales and get to a month and  going so I hope that helps if you guys  liked the video I'd love to see you give  it a thumb  it makes me want to do more of these for  you and if you have a question or you  have something else to add to this video  there to help John out I'd love to see  it below if you wanna leave it in the  comments and we'll see you on the next  episode  [Music]  you  [Music]

